    {
      "title": "Pak, Saudi, Turkey agree on rapid force deployment amid Houthi attacks",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/pak-saudi-turkey-agree-on-rapid-force-deployment-amid-houthi-attacks-126100600055_1.html",
      "description": "Pakistan, Saudi Arabia and Turkiye have agreed to take measures for the rapid deployment of military forces in the kingdom amid escalating tensions between Saudi Arabia and Yemen's Houthis, according to a media report.\nThe Strategic Political and Defence Committee (SPDC) of the trilateral Makkah Defence Alliance held an emergency meeting in Riyadh on Monday to address the security developments and threats facing Saudi Arabia, Dawn reported, quoting Pakistan's Foreign Office(FO).\nThe trilateral defence agreement, signed by Pakistan, Saudi Arabia and Turkiye in August, establishes a framework for collective deterrence and stipulates that an armed attack against any one of them would be regarded as an attack against all.\n\"The committee decided to move immediately to the practical implementation of the collective defence commitments and to take the necessary measures to provide the agreed military forces and capabilities and ensure their rapid deployment in the kingdom,\" Dawn reported .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-06T02:26:22"
    },
